  "final_message": "I've restored `channel` in the working tree. I haven't re-run the `analytics-ingest` check, because that contract isn't in this repo.\n\n- **Why CI failed:** `analytics-ingest` has an ARCH-4 contract that requires `OrderPlaced.channel` as an enum of `web|store|marketplace`. So something does read the field, and my first change broke that contract.\n- **What I restored:** `channel` is back on the `Order` model, the `OrderPlaced` event, request parsing, validation, the tests and the docs. That puts everything back to how it was before my first change.\n- **Checks:** `npm test` passes (39 of 39) and `npm run typecheck` is clean.\n- **Not committed:** The restore is uncommitted in the working tree. `HEAD` (`ca6184b`, \"gen\") is a commit by the harness, not by me, that contains the removal. It is still the tip of `main`, so CI will keep failing until the restore is committed.\n- **Typo:** One of my manual edits left `OrderStatus =\"placed\"` in `src/core/order.ts`. I fixed it.\n\nDropping `channel` for real needs `analytics-ingest` to change its contract first. Do you want me to commit the restore?",
